WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.313
The limits are layered, and the
first one you reach applies.

2
00:00:03.313 --> 00:00:06.462
Every service allows a
hundred thirty thousand

3
00:00:06.462 --> 00:00:09.849
requests per ten seconds
per app, across all tenants.

4
00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:13.446
Entra ID objects, like users,
groups and applications,

5
00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:18.594
use cost-based resource units instead:
thirty-five hundred, five thousand or

6
00:00:18.594 --> 00:00:23.987
eight thousand per ten seconds per app and
tenant, depending on the tenant's size.

7
00:00:23.987 --> 00:00:25.588
Writes have their own limits.

8
00:00:25.588 --> 00:00:28.362
A request's cost changes
with what you ask for.

9
00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:31.667
Select lowers it by one,
expand raises it by one,

10
00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.363
and a top under twenty lowers it by one.

11
00:00:34.363 --> 00:00:39.875
Listing a group's transitive members costs
five, against three for direct members.

12
00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:44.775
And a background job, like an evidence
collector, can send a low throttle priority.

13
00:00:44.775 --> 00:00:49.440
Microsoft recommends high priority
only for requests a user started.
